174:- Client DELETE decision: refused for everyone (own-row DELETE policy dropped; DELETE/TRUNCATE revoked from 
anon/authenticated on conversation_members and conversations); no client "leave". A service-role DELETE is an 
administrative revocation recorded in `private.conversation_member_revocations` (AFTER DELETE trigger, skipping FK 
cascades); only the service_role RPC `public.restore_conversation_membership(uuid,uuid)` lifts a revocation (branches 
on conversation type first: room conversations re-check room rules under lock and a room conversation whose space was 
deleted raises ROOM_NOT_FOUND keeping the revocation; direct/group restore only original participants). No route calls 
restore today; the T24 re-add fixture should use it.
175-- Inventory → decision:
176-  1. Client INSERT/UPSERT on conversation_members → closed: anon INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE revoked; 
authenticated INSERT policy requires `user_id = private.current_app_user_id()` and an existing membership; BEFORE 
INSERT guard lets API roles insert only an already-existing row (FOR KEY SHARE), so old builds' upserts of existing 
rows work and a concurrently deleted row is never re-created (42501 NOT_PARTICIPANT). Trusted (definer/admin) inserts 
pass the insertion-boundary check: lock existing row, raise MEMBERSHIP_REVOKED if a revocation exists — after every 
authorization wait; it never clears revocations.
177-  2. Client UPDATE moving a row → closed: UPDATE policy USING + WITH CHECK own row; trigger makes 
id/conversation_id/user_id immutable for every role.
178-  3. Client DELETE → closed (refused).
179-  4. conversations INSERT by clients → kept (every build's resolver creates with the user-scoped client) but 
authorized by a BEFORE INSERT trigger under row locks: direct = caller + exactly one other existing user under the 
resolver's company rule, no room_id, visibility direct; room = participants exactly [caller] and the room access rules 
(SQL mirror of `assertRoomAccess`, JS-truthiness via `private.jsonb_js_truthy`, out-of-range numbers → 
ROOM_ACL_INVALID deny); group/other refused.
180-  5. conversations UPDATE by clients → only name/last_activity/is_archived (column grants); 
participants/room_id/type/visibility/fingerprint no longer client-writable.
