1025: comment on function public.create_message_attempt(uuid, uuid, text, text, uuid, uuid, bigint, jsonb, uuid[], 
integer, integer) is
1026:   'Phase 5 T2/T3: creates a text message (keyed or not), or a message with 1-5 pending uploads of its sender 
(Phase 4 T12/T15 rules), committing only when the attempt generation is current for (sender, conversation, key) at 
commit time (a generation-less keyed create only when no fence state exists). A winning insertion charges the 
sender''s ''message:create'' insertion quota (p_insert_quota_limit per p_insert_quota_window_seconds; both NULL = no 
charge) in the same transaction: RATE_LIMITED (quota exhausted) or RATE_LIMIT_UNAVAILABLE (charge failed) roll it 
back. Returns {message_id, created, composition, message}; message is the created row (created=true only); 
created=false is a replay (never charged). Raises NOT_PARTICIPANT (42501) for a non-member sender, ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED 
when fenced and MESSAGE_DELETED when a generation-carrying create would recreate a deleted message. Service role only; 
callers authorize the sender and validate the attachment policy first.';
